  "summary": "The Foster City Council approved 4-1 an Automated License Plate Reader program with Flock, installing 20 cameras at city entry/exit points to address rising vehicle thefts and burglaries. Officials said data would be retained 30 days and not used for facial recognition, immigration enforcement, or traffic enforcement, while some council members and residents raised privacy concerns.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "The data would not be used for facial recognition software, immigration enforcement or traffic enforcement, according to John Anderson, territory manager with FlockGroup, Inc.",
      "paragraph_idx": 11
    },
    {
      "quote": "Avelar said the ALPR data would not be stored or retained by the police department or any vendor beyond 30 days, nor would it be warehoused with any private company data.",
      "paragraph_idx": 10
    },
    {
      "quote": "The motion passed 4-1, with Sullivan voting against.",
      "paragraph_idx": 18
    }
  ],
